<title>NORWAY: Norway Seafoods seeks Oslo bourse listing.</title>
<headline>Norway Seafoods seeks Oslo bourse listing.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway Seafoods, the fisheries division of Aker RGI ASA, said on Wednesday it would seek a listing on the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>In a statement to the bourse, Norway Seafoods said the group planned to widen distribution of its stock without issuing new shares.</p>
<p>Aker RGI owns 54.8 percent of Norway Seafoods, the world's largest operator in catching and processing white fish.</p>
<p>&quot;AKER RGI...has no plans to reduce its stake in the company once it has been listed on the bourse,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>Norway Seafoods said it would provide a time frame for the listing at a later date.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
